  "searchProcedure": {
    "implementation": "fit/search.py (pinned by part 1), fit/fit.py",
    "text": "W45's procedure: within a stage, its families are sequential components in familyOrder, each swept on the stage's scope from the point the previous left; within a family each leaf's grid is swept in the order listed, the others held at their current values, at most two passes; a factorialGroups entry sweeps its keys' grid product as ONE coordinate step; a grid point outside a declared joint domain (domainLowerIsMinus) is not a candidate; every step's candidates include the step's start (already measured), so a sweep never forces a move off the incumbent.",
    "tieRule": "points whose objective lies within the stage tie of the step's minimum are indistinguishable; among them the point nearest the step's start wins (the sum over the step's keys of |v - v0| / (domain hi - lo)), then fewer moved leaves, then grid order; the stage decision applies the same rule measured from the stage base. The tie is rule.stage_tie computed once on the stage's declared cells from the reference's own cut (stage 1 0.0365, stage 2 0.0544), never from a point's partial render (the W44 and W45 tracker entries).",
    "objective": "rule.stage_objective: W44's selection metric (median |log(web/native)| over F, C and P) on the stage's cells, both dark scales pooled, the gate partition; a partial objective is never ranked (recover.py, or refusal)",
    "scaleSeparableRendering": "a point's render at one scale is its scale twin's: the point's overrides restricted to the leaves acting at that scale (fit/labels.json `scales`); points whose scale twins have equal resolved digests share that scale's render. Exact under the scale anchoring, which ladders (ii) and (iii) read on every lever (its other scale byte-identical to the control's).",
    "renders": "every fit render in candidate mode on the WebGPU tier with --alpha, through with-gpu.sh; each scope's cells are the dark T1 gate cells of its pose plus L1's declared population of that pose"
  },
  "selectionRule": {
    "withinAStage": "the stage's point with a passing within clause (rule.stage_within: every target cell of the stage within) and the smallest stage objective lands",
    "ifNotWithin": "else the smallest stage objective, an indistinguishable plateau decided by the tie rule from the stage base; recorded as NOT within"
  },
  "interactions": "stage 1's moves of the floors, the 1x heavy tap, the second tap and the gain reach the inactive cells by inheritance and are read there; stage 2 materialises them at the stage-1 active's resolved values (materialiseX64) and holds or moves them independently. The joint point is re-read on the whole gate population (search.py full on the landed point); a stage that undid the other (a cell of the other stage's within clause that its landed point left within is a miss at the final point) is refitted once on the union.",
  "level": "the transmission's domain is ladder (i)'s passing rungs (part 2 narrows each tintAlpha grid to them); every fit scope carries L1's declared population, read at every point, and the gate reads L1 and every other adopted row on the shipped bytes (X61)",
